</address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MOTOYOSHI KANAME</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUMOTO, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIDAKA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOTOYOSHI, KANAME</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A first low-noise amplifier (LNA1 111) includes a control terminal (1115) for turn it ON and OFF. The first low-noise amplifier (LNA1 111) and a second low-noise amplifier (LNA2 112) have their respective power terminal connected together to a power supply (10) through a power supply switch (1114). The two amplifiers (LNA1 111, LNA2 112) have ground terminals connected together to ground through a constant current source (1 115). When the voltage applied to the control terminal (1115) of the first low-noise amplifier (LNA1 111) is switched HIGH and LOW, both of the amplifiers (LNA1 111, LNA2 112) turn ON and OFF. The power supply switch (1114) is OFF for transmitting a signal. As a result, a LNA block can be composed of a single power supply switch (1114), decreasing the number of components and realizing a compact device.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un premier amplificateur à faible bruit (LNA1 111) comprenant un terminal de commande (1115) pour l'ouvrir ou le fermer. Ledit amplificateur (LNA1 111) et un second amplificateur à faible bruit (LNA2 112) ont chacun leur terminal électrique relié à une alimentation électrique (10) au moyen d'un commutateur d'alimentation (1114). Les deux amplificateurs ((LNA1 111, LNA2 112) ont des prises de terre reliées à la terre par une source de courant constante (1 115). Lorsque la tension appliquée au terminal de commande (1115) du premier amplificateur à faible bruit (LNA1 111) est commutée HAUTE et BASSE, les deux amplificateurs (LNA1 111, (LNA2 112) s'ouvrent et se ferment. Le commutateur d'alimentation (1114) se ferme pour l'émission d'un signal. Il en résulte qu'un bloc LNA peut comporter un seul commutateur d'alimentation (1114), ce qui permet de réduire le nombre de composants et de réaliser un dispositif compact.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>